The `jni` package's android/build.gradle has:
``
externalNativeBuild {
   cmake {
       // The default CMake version for the Android Gradle Plugin is 3.10.2.
       // https://developer.android.com/studio/projects/install-ndk#vanilla_cmake
       // ... version "3.10.2" (commented out)
   }
``

So the PR's claim about the commented-out version line is TRUE — verified locally in the pub cache at `~/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/jni-1.1.0/android/build.gradle` lines 55-65.

Note the comment says "The default CMake version for the Android Gradle Plugin is 3.10.2" — that comment is stale (from older AGP days), but the actual behavior matters: what IS the AGP default CMake version? For modern AGP (4.1+ through 8.x, and presumably 9.x), the default CMake version is 3.22.1. The AGP source (Cmake.java / CmakeUtils) pins "3.22.1" as `DEFAULT_CMAKE_VERSION` since AGP 4.2/7.0. For AGP 9.0.1, I need to verify — the CI failure log itself said `Failed to install the following SDK components: cmake;3.22.1`, which is ground truth: AGP 9.0.1 requested cmake;3.22.1. So the coupling claim is verified by the actual CI failure (v1.0.619) — AGP 9.0.1 requested cmake;3.22.1.

